                <h1 class="detail-page__title h2">
                    AFRC and SFC extend regulatory cooperation to financial reporting of licensed firms and funds under new MoU
                </h1>

                                    <ul class="detail-page__info-list">
                                                    <li class="detail-page__info-item">
                                <p class="detail-page__info detail-page__info--date">
                                    28 September 2026
                                </p>
                            </li>
                                                                                            </ul>
                            </div>
        </div>

                    <div class="detail-page__highlight component-blk">
                <div class="container container--narrow">
                    <div class="detail-page-img-txt img-txt img-txt--bp-lg img-txt--center img-txt--nowrap" >
        <div class="img-txt__inner detail-page-img-txt__inner">
                    <div class="img-txt__side detail-page-img-txt__side">
                                    <div class="detail-page__highlight-img-wrap">
                                        <div
    class="img-thumb detail-page__highlight-img"
    style="--aspect-ratio:1.7722;"
>
                            <picture><source srcset="/f/pressrelease/1536/879p496/WWW00601.webp 1x, /f/pressrelease/1536/1758p992/WWW00601.webp 2x" type="image/webp"><img src="/f/pressrelease/1536/879p496/WWW00601.jpg" class="img-thumb__img" alt="mou" loading="lazy"></picture>
            </div>
    
                                        
                                        <div
    class="img-thumb detail-page__highlight-img detail-page__highlight-img--bg-overlay"
    style="--aspect-ratio:1.7722;" aria-hidden="true"
>
                            <picture><source srcset="/f/pressrelease/1536/879p496/WWW00601.webp 1x, /f/pressrelease/1536/1758p992/WWW00601.webp 2x" type="image/webp"><img src="/f/pressrelease/1536/879p496/WWW00601.jpg" class="img-thumb__img" alt="mou" loading="lazy"></picture>
            </div>
                                    </div>
                
                            </div>
                    </div>
    
</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        
        <div data-component-name="prj_01" id="bb6abf">
    <div class="basic-component component-blk">
        <div
            class="container container--narrow"
            data-aos="fade-up"
            data-aos-duration="1000"
        >
            
            <div class="basic-component-img-txt img-txt img-txt--bp-md img-txt--left img-txt--nowrap" >
        <div class="img-txt__inner basic-component-img-txt__inner">
                            <div class="img-txt__content basic-component-img-txt__content">
                <div class="img-txt__content-inner basic-component-img-txt__content-inner">
                    <div class="ck-content">
                <p>The Accounting and Financial Reporting Council (AFRC) and the Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) today entered into a new <a href="https://www.afrc.org.hk/f/upload/1122/MOU_SFC_AFRC_2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Memorandum of Understanding (MoU)</a> to expand regulatory cooperation beyond the oversight of financial reporting and related audit work of listed entities (Note 1).<br>&nbsp;</p><p>The new MoU covers the financial and compliance reporting by licensed corporations, SFC-licensed virtual asset service providers, SFC-authorised funds and registered open-ended fund companies, as well as the related audit and assurance work performed by their auditors. &nbsp;In addition, it establishes a comprehensive framework for information sharing, case referrals, mutual assistance, and coordinated inspections and investigations in matters of mutual regulatory interest.<br>&nbsp;</p><p>Dr David Sun, Chairman of the AFRC, said, “This MoU marks an important milestone in the longstanding partnership between the AFRC and the SFC. &nbsp;By providing a clearer framework for coordination, it strengthens our collective ability to safeguard the public interest and support the continued resilience and long-term competitiveness of Hong Kong’s financial markets.”<br>&nbsp;</p><p>Dr Kelvin Wong, Chairman of the SFC, said, “This MoU reinforces our shared commitment to reliable financial reporting and high-quality audits. Closer collaboration with the AFRC to cover a broader range of entities and activities in our diverse financial ecosystem will ensure more comprehensive oversight, strengthening market integrity and consolidating Hong Kong’s standing as a trusted international financial centre.”<br>&nbsp;</p><p>Ms Janey Lai, Chief Executive Officer of the AFRC, said, “Reliable financial reporting and auditing underpin market integrity and investor confidence. The enhanced cooperation and information sharing between the AFRC and the SFC will enable us to identify emerging risks earlier and carry out our statutory responsibilities to respond more effectively.”&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</p><p>Ms Julia Leung, Chief Executive Officer of the SFC, said, “This MoU strengthens regulatory backing for our collaboration with the AFRC, ensuring our supervision evolves with market dynamics. Deepening our regulatory cooperation across financial sub-sectors is essential to upholding the quality of financial reporting and bolstering the confidence of global investors in Hong Kong’s regulatory system.”</p><p><br>Note:<br>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The new MoU supersedes the one signed between the SFC and the former Financial Reporting Council in 2021.<br>&nbsp;</p>
    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            </div>
    
</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


